{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1552815-void-spirits","id":1552815,"title":"Void Spirits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-08-01T16:49:37-07:00","id":1552815,"title":"Void Spirits","content":"Doing a short chronicle (first werewolf, not first in chronicles though) as a pre-amble to a bigger one later.<br /> <br /> It's going to be about the Gauntlet falling in Australia after a Void Spirit crashes down there. A cult of Beshilu happen upon it, and form a bizarre fusion. They change rapidly and spread throughout the continent quickly, and by the time any Forsaken realize the problem it's too late, the Gauntlet falls.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping for more inspiration for Void spirits, and how they might mutate and change a Shartha, I've read the bit in Shunned by the Moon, but was wanting for more examples of anyone has any.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28042-rexitonic","name":"Rexitonic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28042_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-02T16:39:21-07:00","id":1552844,"title":"","content":"Without further information on the narrative space the mutant Hosts are intended to fill, I don't know that there's much to offer besides throwing stuff at the wall to see what sticks, because you're describing a highly aberrant circumstance that exists as a prelude to a setting-altering event on a disastrous scale.<br /> <br /> When you say &quot;a void spirit,&quot; is this a &quot;typical&quot; specimen whose place in the metaphysical train derailment is simply that it dropped close enough to the nest and far enough from werewolf intervention for this to happen? Is it a champion of the <i>gasuhathim</i> serving some specific agenda? Does it have a unique trait or power that caused this to happen? Is it more properly a void leviathan making landfall in the same genre of catastrophic world-poisoning as is typical but with extra extradimensional rat-people?<br /> <br /> Are the <i>shartha</i> still adhering to their normal ratlike/humanoid body plan or are things getting weirder in line with the spiritual blight void spirits spread? Is their focus on black-eyed contagion or fleeing the sinking ship of their old nests or tearing open passages between more worlds than usual? How much are they diverging from the standard Fleshy nature of the &quot;species&quot; versus the darkness and unreality found in, say, a void reiver?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-02T20:31:58-07:00","id":1552846,"title":"","content":"My PC blue screened when writing my original reply! Yay!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1552815-void-spirits?p=1552844#post1552844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without further information on the narrative space the mutant Hosts are intended to fill, I don't know that there's much to offer besides throwing stuff at the wall to see what sticks, because you're describing a highly aberrant circumstance that exists as a prelude to a setting-altering event on a disastrous scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay so, cutting things short cause I don't want to type out my original message all over again!<br /> The main purpose of this specific prelude, is to try to interact with a friend who moved away, and prepare myself for running the larger chronicle. The larger chronicle is going to consist of three stories around the pack. Story one, is to be a very short introduction to the Uratha for that group, who will be different. Story two, is going to be the main chunk of the chronicle, this is a Mad Max-esque of car fights (with werewolves) and post apocalyptic survival, the players will have a Totem that's been infused with a big awesome war machine, like in Mad Max, and an &quot;Enclave&quot;, a base of operations and relative safety for their pack, and possibly others. Over the course of story 2, they'll be going around surviving, gathering resources, allies what have you, and during that time they'll slowly begin to learn what exactly happened, coming across aberrant <i>Beshilu </i>nest in various states, ranging from expired, &quot;dormant&quot;, or active. Story 3 will be them participating in a grand ritual to end the Void Spirit and exterminate the mutated <i>Shartha</i>, working together with established allies and others who've been working in the background.<br /> The prelude will be the early onset of the <i>Shartha </i>incursion, a bit of a tragedy where despite their efforts locally, the problem is already too widespread in the country, and the Gauntlet there snaps.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1552815-void-spirits?p=1552844#post1552844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you say &quot;a void spirit,&quot; is this a &quot;typical&quot; specimen whose place in the metaphysical train derailment is simply that it dropped close enough to the nest and far enough from werewolf intervention for this to happen? Is it a champion of the <i>gasuhathim</i> serving some specific agenda? Does it have a unique trait or power that caused this to happen? Is it more properly a void leviathan making landfall in the same genre of catastrophic world-poisoning as is typical but with extra extradimensional rat-people?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, my most basic, original thought, was a Void Leviathan, but clearly I'm not 100% set or sure. Australia is big and empty, I'm thinking something disrupted and prevented intervention, a mixture of the Void spirit landing somewhere isolated and difficult to reach, and/or, for some reason, having been undetected. Exact... capabilities I'm really not sure of, half the reason for this whole specific post. Going for Cosmic Horror, maybe Color out of Space type stuff, Annihilation, ect. I think a champion of a <i>gasuhathim</i> could make a lot of sense for as to how it somehow didn't get prevented before shit hit the fan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1552815-void-spirits?p=1552844#post1552844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the <i>shartha</i> still adhering to their normal ratlike/humanoid body plan or are things getting weirder in line with the spiritual blight void spirits spread? Is their focus on black-eyed contagion or fleeing the sinking ship of their old nests or tearing open passages between more worlds than usual? How much are they diverging from the standard Fleshy nature of the &quot;species&quot; versus the darkness and unreality found in, say, a void reiver?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking that the <i>Shartha </i>slowly get worse and worse as time goes on, originally, for the prelude, they're relatively &quot;normal&quot; for <i>Beshilu</i>. Fleshy body horror of being controlled by rats, feverish apocalyptic cult doing its business. But theres things different going on, they're destroying the Gauntlet faster than they should be able to normally, and they activate Auspice modifications that Uratha get in the presence of Void Spirits. Initially, they encounter the more standard rat host, but near the end of the short chronicle, they'll get... voidy woidy.<br /> So, with that, their focus is that initial, basic, bringing down the Gauntlet so that they may rejoin as the Plague King. They're only able to get it down in Australia, so over the course of the longer chronicle, they'll be doing <i>something</i> big, and that'll be part of the hints, and that pack slowly uncovers the mutated hosts and see signs of some grander, more focused goal.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28042,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28042-rexitonic","user":"Rexitonic","date":". 08-02-2025, 11:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28042-rexitonic","name":"Rexitonic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28042_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-03T08:53:13-07:00","id":1552854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rexitonic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1552815-void-spirits?p=1552846#post1552846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main purpose of this specific prelude, is to try to interact with a friend who moved away, and prepare myself for running the larger chronicle. The larger chronicle is going to consist of three stories around the pack. Story one, is to be a very short introduction to the Uratha for that group, who will be different. Story two, is going to be the main chunk of the chronicle, this is a Mad Max-esque of car fights (with werewolves) and post apocalyptic survival, the players will have a Totem that's been infused with a big awesome war machine, like in Mad Max, and an &quot;Enclave&quot;, a base of operations and relative safety for their pack, and possibly others. Over the course of story 2, they'll be going around surviving, gathering resources, allies what have you, and during that time they'll slowly begin to learn what exactly happened, coming across aberrant <i>Beshilu </i>nest in various states, ranging from expired, &quot;dormant&quot;, or active. Story 3 will be them participating in a grand ritual to end the Void Spirit and exterminate the mutated <i>Shartha</i>, working together with established allies and others who've been working in the background.<br /> The prelude will be the early onset of the <i>Shartha </i>incursion, a bit of a tragedy where despite their efforts locally, the problem is already too widespread in the country, and the Gauntlet there snaps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems a solid structure, although from a pacing perspective &quot;Story 2&quot; might more properly be considered as multiple stories, depending on how much focus is being given on individual large acquisitions of resources and allies; speaking as someone who made the mistake of combining a PC group's introductory story with an assignment from on high that turned out more complicated than it seemed, being able to parcel out narrative beats so that, say, the major cornerstones of Story 3's grand ritual feel like more than just MacGuffins and the pack won't have to ration their ability to flare their Renown will be helpful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, my most basic, original thought, was a Void Leviathan, but clearly I'm not 100% set or sure. Australia is big and empty, I'm thinking something disrupted and prevented intervention, a mixture of the Void spirit landing somewhere isolated and difficult to reach, and/or, for some reason, having been undetected. Exact... capabilities I'm really not sure of, half the reason for this whole specific post. Going for Cosmic Horror, maybe Color out of Space type stuff, Annihilation, ect. I think a champion of a <i>gasuhathim</i> could make a lot of sense for as to how it somehow didn't get prevented before shit hit the fan. </div> </div> </div>I'd also probably recommend the champion angle, if only because unless you intend to make a thematic statement on the truly apocalyptically bad luck it would take for this to happen coincidentally it'll help to have a background agenda this is meant to serve that can be thwarted. On the other hand, freak coincidence means you don't have to worry as much about what's stopping this from happening again, which a mastermind beneath the arches of the night sky theoretically does (albeit in terms that can readily include &quot;this was the product of a lot of variables being tweaked just so over a long period of time&quot;).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was thinking that the <i>Shartha </i>slowly get worse and worse as time goes on, originally, for the prelude, they're relatively &quot;normal&quot; for <i>Beshilu</i>. Fleshy body horror of being controlled by rats, feverish apocalyptic cult doing its business. But theres things different going on, they're destroying the Gauntlet faster than they should be able to normally, and they activate Auspice modifications that Uratha get in the presence of Void Spirits. Initially, they encounter the more standard rat host, but near the end of the short chronicle, they'll get... voidy woidy.<br /> So, with that, their focus is that initial, basic, bringing down the Gauntlet so that they may rejoin as the Plague King. They're only able to get it down in Australia, so over the course of the longer chronicle, they'll be doing <i>something</i> big, and that'll be part of the hints, and that pack slowly uncovers the mutated hosts and see signs of some grander, more focused goal. </div> </div> </div>Something that's probably worth thinking about is that, while obviously coming up with new effects is directly encouraged, the list of example Spirit Blight effects is kind of tilted in the opposite direction from what the Beshilu do to the Gauntlet; taking the description in the &quot;Hunting the Gauntlet&quot; sidebar and the modifications void spirits make to void reivers as a starting point, leaning into the emptiness and alien inhospitability angles is probably the right way to go, since hunger and disease are motifs that sort of race each other to the end of their bearers' lives without the functional immortality common to the Shadow.<br /> <br /> You might give the mutant Beshilu Dread Powers with effects similar to the Facets of the Gift of Hunger, render the infected Shards semi-contagious, or take some cues from Shunned's mechanics for Wounds (or the corebook's Essence Shaping powers from the idigam) to apply to loci and other areas affected by the Hosts' gnawing. It may be worth addressing, if this isn't simply a common train of thought being hijacked by the void, how the rats think the Gauntlet as a whole is in the way of their reunion \u2014 The Sundered World says that Rat once carved out a warren of tunnels in Pangaea and filled them with beautiful things, so perhaps there's something stuck in the Gauntlet somewhere (probably somewhere thick, if you'd like to lean into the impact on major population centers) that can only be reached by tearing it all down?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T01:37:38-07:00","id":1552875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1552815-void-spirits?p=1552854#post1552854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems a solid structure, although from a pacing perspective &quot;Story 2&quot; might more properly be considered as multiple stories, depending on how much focus is being given on individual large acquisitions of resources and allies; speaking as someone who made the mistake of combining a PC group's introductory story with an assignment from on high that turned out more complicated than it seemed, being able to parcel out narrative beats so that, say, the major cornerstones of Story 3's grand ritual feel like more than just MacGuffins and the pack won't have to ration their ability to flare their Renown will be helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely something I'll take into mind. Might, for my own internal structures sake, rename Story 2 and 3 as Arcs, then just have individual stories contained within.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1552815-void-spirits?p=1552854#post1552854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also probably recommend the champion angle, if only because unless you intend to make a thematic statement on the truly apocalyptically bad luck it would take for this to happen coincidentally it'll help to have a background agenda this is meant to serve that can be thwarted. On the other hand, freak coincidence means you don't have to worry as much about what's stopping this from happening again, which a mastermind beneath the arches of the night sky theoretically does (albeit in terms that can readily include &quot;this was the product of a lot of variables being tweaked just so over a long period of time&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll probably go the champion angle then, makes it a bit easier for the whole, insidious threat in waiting bit, and how they got by everything. I saw this post, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1132350-eclipses-and-their-ramifications-regarding-the-hisil-its-inhabitants-et-al\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...abitants-et-al</a>, saying that Luna is &quot;blind&quot; during a Lunar Eclipse. Either way, the story is &quot;self-contained&quot;, it doesn't affect the other chronicles the group will play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1552815-void-spirits?p=1552854#post1552854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that's probably worth thinking about is that, while obviously coming up with new effects is directly encouraged, the list of example Spirit Blight effects is kind of tilted in the opposite direction from what the Beshilu do to the Gauntlet; taking the description in the &quot;Hunting the Gauntlet&quot; sidebar and the modifications void spirits make to void reivers as a starting point, leaning into the emptiness and alien inhospitability angles is probably the right way to go, since hunger and disease are motifs that sort of race each other to the end of their bearers' lives without the functional immortality common to the Shadow.<br /> <br /> You might give the mutant Beshilu Dread Powers with effects similar to the Facets of the Gift of Hunger, render the infected Shards semi-contagious, or take some cues from Shunned's mechanics for Wounds (or the corebook's Essence Shaping powers from the idigam) to apply to loci and other areas affected by the Hosts' gnawing. It may be worth addressing, if this isn't simply a common train of thought being hijacked by the void, how the rats think the Gauntlet as a whole is in the way of their reunion \u2014 The Sundered World says that Rat once carved out a warren of tunnels in Pangaea and filled them with beautiful things, so perhaps there's something stuck in the Gauntlet somewhere (probably somewhere thick, if you'd like to lean into the impact on major population centers) that can only be reached by tearing it all down?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Lots of useful tips here, nothing to say in particular, much appreciated. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I can definitely see me taking that last sentence into account especially.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28042-rexitonic","name":"Rexitonic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28042_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-06T20:45:41-07:00","id":1552967,"title":"","content":"Wrote this for myself as a retainer of thoughts and ideas, helps me get a mood. It was SUPPOSED to be from the perspective of a Beshilu minister figure, but uh, apparently I have a hard time actually writing in a more maddened fanatic method! So I ended up altering the perspective to be a bit more omniscient.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The firmament of night was darker and blacker, it was inky and beautiful, the stars shown brightly in the Outback. Luna\u2019s face was hidden. Her senses blind.<br /> <br /> That was when it landed, a spirit from beyond even her. It came unto their nest, and it spoke in garbled speech, pain wrenching, disgusting, but familiar speech. They knew not what it said, but understood it nonetheless.<br /> <br /> And so, they partook its flesh, a communion of the void, of the greater beyond, and it instilled a great, furious, empty hunger upon on nest.<br /> <br /> And so, they spread. They gnawed at the walls between with greater fervor than ever before. They spread more, they gnawed more. They spread and gnawed, the wolves could scarce believe it as it was happening, as it all fell crashing and crumbling and collapsing down. The Uratha couldn\u2019t prevent us, it was far, far too late. The one from beyond promises them that their eternal hunger to once again be the great king of plagues to be satisfied. To overwhelm the scions of Urfarah, their great nests re-united.<br /> <br /> The Gauntlet of Australia fell. And so they wait. In hiding, for command and purpose. Changing ever dimmer, ever emptier, ever hungrier. In absent abandon.</b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28042-rexitonic","name":"Rexitonic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28042_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-07T23:06:48-07:00","id":1553000,"title":"","content":"Honestly, thinking of just making the big bad an Idigam with a HEAVY amount of Void Influence on them. Maybe when Father wolf tossed him to luna, he missed and we went passed her or something idk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28042-rexitonic","name":"Rexitonic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28042_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-08T06:01:52-07:00","id":1553009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rexitonic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1552815-void-spirits?p=1553000#post1553000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, thinking of just making the big bad an Idigam with a HEAVY amount of Void Influence on them. Maybe when Father wolf tossed him to luna, he missed and we went passed her or something idk.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably the better call vis-a-vis using existing tools suited to the beats you're aiming for, yeah; Coalescence in the void making a technical Moon-Banished uniquely suited to tearing down the Gauntlet in a large area needs less structural homebrewing than figuring out unique interactions with disparate monster-types, and there's still room for spiritual politicking with the gasuhathim to be involved thanks to the precedent of idigam riding radio signals back to Earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}